 "encoding": "A Pauli on logical qubits 2..12 is a 22-bit integer: x bits 0..10 (qubit i + 2 in bit i), z bits 11..21. The identity is 0. A transvection by a native rotation g maps p to p ^ g when p and g anticommute (symplectic product 1) and fixes p otherwise. For Q = X, Y, Z the histograms cover all 4^11 Paulis (the identity costs beta = 1: Q alone is native); for Q = I the identity I (x) I is no measurement and is left out, so those histograms cover 4^11 - 1 Paulis (see `total`).",
 "readings": {
  "hypothetical245": "if every shift acted as A (+) A, as p. 47 of the paper states; 245 rotations",
  "rotations245": "the engine's shift action (A (+) A^T on logical qubits 7-12); rotations about native Paulis whose pivot letter is X, Y or Z (Eq. 15 as printed)",
  "rotations510": "the same shift action with the pivot letter I allowed in the rotations (the 510 the paper's text counts)"
 },
